{"sourceSha256": "6514a400d6f759f5b539c95a61bab8a09908bcaad3dbec8183bf71b86be5f34b", "text": "Nurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nyoung, and I just don’t know what to do.\n\nI know this comes as a shock to you, | also understand how worrying\nit must be. | am here to reassure you that he's going to be okay and\nwill make a complete recovery soon.\n\n| am so confused... | thought it was just the flu. He wasn’t recovering,\nso I brought him here to see if it was something serious. And now the\ndoctor says it’s a brain tumour. It's shocking!\n\nYes, regrettably it’s crue. The presenting symptoms were similar to the\nflu, but the investigations have confirmed the diagnosis of a tumour in\nhis head. In Jimmy's case, it was the pressure at the back of his head\ncausing the headaches. You did the right thing by bringing him to the\nhospital today.\n\nTell me, is he going to be okay?\n\nYes, the doctor is highly skilled, and Jimmy will receive the best\npossible care in this hospital. He will be able to recuperate soon.\nWhere is Jimmy at the moment? | haven't seen him at all since\nmorning. It's been 5 hours. The doctor said | cannot see him for\nanother hour,\n\nI understand your concern, Mrs Anderson. | apologise for the fact that\nyou had to wait so long. Jimmy had to be sedated so he could remain\nstill for the MRI scan procedure. Right now, he's in the ward and is\nbeing closely monitored by our staff. You will be able to see him\nshortly.\n\nOh... Lam in shock! | cannot think straight at the moment.\n\n| know you are overwhelmed. Take your time to process this\ninformation, And let me know if you have any questions about what\nyou have been told.\n\nSo, the doctor says Jimmy needs surgery. It's just so scary co think that\nmy little boy is going to be operated upon. Is the surgery dangerous?\n\n| know it’s a lot to take in. The doctor has advised a surgery because a\ntumour needs to be removed from Jimmy's head. There is nothing to\nbe alarmed about the surgery as your son is safe hands. Following the\nsurgery, he will be monitored for a week in the hospital to check\nprogress in his condition,", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Nurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nMother:\n\nNurse:\n\nyoung, and I just don’t know what to do.\n\nI know this comes as a shock to you, | also understand how worrying\nit must be. | am here to reassure you that he's going to be okay and\nwill make a complete recovery soon.\n\n| am so confused... | thought it was just the flu. He wasn’t recovering,\nso I brought him here to see if it was something serious. And now the\ndoctor says it’s a brain tumour. It's shocking!\n\nYes, regrettably it’s crue. The presenting symptoms were similar to the\nflu, but the investigations have confirmed the diagnosis of a tumour in\nhis head. In Jimmy's case, it was the pressure at the back of his head\ncausing the headaches. You did the right thing by bringing him to the\nhospital today.\n\nTell me, is he going to be okay?\n\nYes, the doctor is highly skilled, and Jimmy will receive the best\npossible care in this hospital. He will be able to recuperate soon.\nWhere is Jimmy at the moment? | haven't seen him at all since\nmorning. It's been 5 hours. The doctor said | cannot see him for\nanother hour,\n\nI understand your concern, Mrs Anderson. | apologise for the fact that\nyou had to wait so long. Jimmy had to be sedated so he could remain\nstill for the MRI scan procedure. Right now, he's in the ward and is\nbeing closely monitored by our staff. You will be able to see him\nshortly.\n\nOh... Lam in shock! | cannot think straight at the moment.\n\n| know you are overwhelmed. Take your time to process this\ninformation, And let me know if you have any questions about what\nyou have been told.\n\nSo, the doctor says Jimmy needs surgery. It's just so scary co think that\nmy little boy is going to be operated upon. Is the surgery dangerous?\n\n| know it’s a lot to take in. The doctor has advised a surgery because a\ntumour needs to be removed from Jimmy's head. There is nothing to\nbe alarmed about the surgery as your son is safe hands. Following the\nsurgery, he will be monitored for a week in the hospital to check\nprogress in his condition,", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2220.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Nurse:", "lines": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.13786, "width": 0.06081, "height": 0.01321, "confidence": 0.967, "words": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "width": 0.06081, "confidence": 0.967}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Mother:", "lines": [{"text": "Mother:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.2075, "width": 0.07568, "height": 0.01393, "confidence": 0.961, "words": [{"text": "Mother:", "x": 0.13063, "width": 0.07568, "confidence": 0.961}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Nurse:", "lines": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.27857, "width": 0.06081, "height": 0.01321, "confidence": 0.964, "words": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "width": 0.06081, "confidence": 0.964}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Mother:", "lines": [{"text": "Mother:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.39321, "width": 0.07568, "height": 0.01357, "confidence": 0.965, "words": [{"text": "Mother:", "x": 0.13063, "width": 0.07568, "confidence": 0.965}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Nurse:", "lines": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.42, "width": 0.06081, "height": 0.01321, "confidence": 0.952, "words": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "width": 0.06081, "confidence": 0.952}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Mother:", "lines": [{"text": "Mother:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.46821, "width": 0.07568, "height": 0.01393, "confidence": 0.965, "words": [{"text": "Mother:", "x": 0.13063, "width": 0.07568, "confidence": 0.965}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Nurse:", "lines": [{"text": "Nurse:", "x": 0.13063, "y": 0.53857, "width